ref 17592186499694} {:answer/id #uuid "5b711e67-6b4c-5419-a74e-8098d5c2e1ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{28}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499831} {:answer/id #uuid "647448d8-c56e-561c-a3d4-59317e57f4ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{35}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499849} {:answer/id #uuid "a811a50d-2956-506e-b098-0bd862fe0b17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499981} {:answer/id #uuid "ac4dfbc5-e90c-545e-ba5d-eddfa04b9910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a811a50d-2956-506e-b098-0bd862fe0b17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499981} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cc12287-be31-553d-911e-bf2ff3aa5cd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500200}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bd4ff006-9ebf-5a4d-9116-4f5cd068a5ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-77616" :question/problem "![](images/dc/dc12a180a283b34a36d1f44d6ea197b017138632f1d1918255a1b4253b541fd0.png)\n\nConsider the triangle $△ABC$ shown above. The line segment $\\overset{―}{CH}$ is the altitude corresponding to $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ If $m∠BAC={120}^{∘},$ calculate $m∠HCA.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the straight angle must have a measure of ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠HAC+m∠BAC & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HAC+{120}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HAC & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $△AHC$ is a right triangle. Since its interior angles must sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠HCA+m∠HAC+m∠AHC & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HCA+{60}^{∘}+{90}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HCA+{150}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HCA & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
